@startuml environment-domain
' Editable source for the Environment domain model; not an implementation design.
' Sources: ../SRS.tex G.4, G.6 and S.2 (FR-LVL, FR-CHK, FR-PER, FR-REV).
' Draft reference: C:/Users/itari/Documents/SRS.tex E.1 and E.6.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -tpdf environment-domain.puml
' Preview: java -jar plantuml.jar -tsvg environment-domain.puml
!pragma layout smetana
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam wrapWidth 180
title FPVR course-training domain

class "Virtual environment" as Environment
class "Obstacle-course level" as Course
class "Required checkpoint" as Checkpoint {
  sequence position
}
class "Course attempt" as Attempt {
  completed checkpoint prefix
  total and section elapsed time
  crash count
}
class "Simulated drone" as Drone
class "Completed-attempt review" as Review {
  completion time and checkpoint results
  crash count, score and rating
}

Environment "1" -- "0..*" Course : provides the setting for
Course "1" -- "1..*" Checkpoint : defines an ordered sequence of
Course "1" -- "0..*" Attempt : can be practised through
Attempt "0..*" -- "1" Drone : uses
Attempt "1" -- "0..1" Review : yields on successful completion

note bottom of Attempt
  One current course run; respawn continues it.
  Restart creates a new attempt and resets its data.
  Free flight is outside this course-attempt model.
end note
note bottom of Review
  Completion requires all checkpoints in order,
  followed by the finish. Review covers the current
  completed attempt, independently of optional AI.
end note

legend bottom
  Lines name domain relationships; end labels show multiplicity.
  Multiplicities describe possible interactions, not stored history.
  Classes are concepts, not software modules or database tables.
endlegend
@enduml
